{"seq":2,"slug":"writing-effective-context","title":"Writing Effective Context","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/writing-effective-context","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-to-put-in-agents","title":"AGENTS.md 该写什么","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/writing-effective-context/what-to-put-in-agents","wordCount":1758,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"conventions-and-gotchas","title":"约定与坑","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/writing-effective-context/conventions-and-gotchas","wordCount":1935,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"keeping-it-concise","title":"保持精炼","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/writing-effective-context/keeping-it-concise","wordCount":1823,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<p>本章讲怎么把上下文文件写得真有用。该写什么:agent 最需要、代码里读不出来的——怎么装跑验、技术栈与架构要点、关键约定、已知的坑与禁区、为什么这么设计;别写代码自己能说清的、易过期的细节。约定与坑要写明白:用什么包管理器、命名/分层规矩、&quot;这个命令要先跑那个&quot;&quot;这里很慢别动&quot;,把 agent 反复踩的雷写成显式的禁区。还要保持精炼——上下文文件越长,关键信息越被淹没、越容易过期;聚焦最高频、最要紧的,把&quot;该知道的&quot;压到 agent 一眼能抓住,而非堆成一篇没人读完的长文。</p>\n"}